<title>ITALY: Italy govt partners to discuss jobs not budget.</title>
<headline>Italy govt partners to discuss jobs not budget.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unemployment, not the mini-budget, will be discussed when Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi meets party leaders in his coalition on Thursday, Deputy Prime Minister Walter Veltroni said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are going to talk about employment tomorrow,&quot; Veltroni told reporters when asked if Prodi and his partners planned to discuss the mini-budget which Prodi has said he will unveil in the next few weeks.</p>
<p>--Rome bureau, +39 6 678 2501</p>
</text>
